# The intersection of two intervals with 2-limb bounds (milestone2.md, "One enclosure
# interface"): the listing of interval_intersection_1 on the comparison of two limbs, lt_2_2, each
# bound selected limb by limb, and the empty set ((+inf, 0), (-inf, 0)) when the bounds cross.
# Exact. For every precision.
kernel:        interval_intersection_2
input:         xl = xl0 xl1
input:         xu = xu0 xu1
input:         yl = yl0 yl1
input:         yu = yu0 yu1
output:        zl = zl0 zl1
output:        zu = zu0 zu1
requires:      interval xl xu
requires:      interval yl yu
ensures:       interval_set zl zu intersection x=xl,xu y=yl,yu
min_precision: 1
source:        the larger lower bound and the smaller upper bound by lt_2_2, the empty set if they cross (Milestone 2 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the bounds are selected among the bounds of the operands and the infinities of the empty set; interval_set states what comes out for every pair of canonical intervals

ml  = lt_2_2(xl0, xl1, yl0, yl1)
l0  = select(ml, yl0, xl0)
l1  = select(ml, yl1, xl1)
mu  = lt_2_2(yu0, yu1, xu0, xu1)
h0  = select(mu, yu0, xu0)
h1  = select(mu, yu1, xu1)
ok  = le_2_2(l0, l1, h0, h1)
mi  = neg(const inf)
zl0 = select(ok, l0, const inf)
zl1 = select(ok, l1, 0)
zu0 = select(ok, h0, mi)
zu1 = select(ok, h1, 0)
